# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Mission Control — deploy-only repository
#
# This repo publishes exactly one thing: the GitHub Pages dashboard.
# Everything else in this workspace is local working material — ~31 GB of ad
# media, CRM exports, migration sets, skills, and scripts — and must never be
# committed. Several of those files contain customer contact data.
#
# So the rule is inverted: ignore everything, then explicitly allow the files
# that actually deploy. A new data file can never be committed by accident.
#
# TO PUBLISH A NEW FILE: add an explicit `!filename` line below.
# Root files are load-bearing for the deploy — see CLAUDE.md, "Root Files —
# Do Not Relocate" — so keep this list in sync with that table.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Ignore everything by default.
*

# ── The published site ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
!index.html
!linkedin-walkthrough.html
!hubspot-vs-nooks-slide.html
# Self-contained creative gallery. Thumbnails are inlined as base64 so no ad media
# is tracked. Regenerate with scripts/build_creative_gallery.py.
!creative-gallery.html

# Career Runway outbound sequences. Copy, scoring model and bucket counts only —
# no contact rows. Regenerate with scripts/build_career_runway_page.py.
!career-runway-sequences.html

# PBExpo 2027 registration campaign brief. Ported from the Claude artifact so it is
# viewable without a Claude login. Self-contained — fonts inlined, no scripts.
!filling-the-floor.html

# Dashboard data. dashboard-state.json is fetched as a root sibling by both
# viewers; ad-performance.json is written here by the partsbase-linkedin-ads
# weekday ad-account check.
!dashboard-state.json
!ad-performance.json

# Self-serve email template gallery + builder. The gallery shows a live scaled
# preview of each template and hands off to the builder, which fills in and
# downloads a ready-to-upload HTML file client-side — no backend, nothing
# saved server-side. The master templates are the already-HubSpot-fixed
# campaign HTML files; fields-data.js maps each form field to the element(s)
# it edits in that master, and both pages read it directly.
!template-gallery.html
!template-builder.html
!resources/
!resources/template-builder/
!resources/template-builder/fields-data.js
!resources/template-builder/masters/
!resources/template-builder/masters/pbexpo.html
!resources/template-builder/masters/partstore.html
!resources/template-builder/masters/jumbo.html
!resources/template-builder/masters/networking.html
!resources/template-builder/masters/amelia.html

# ── This file ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Tracked so the protection survives a fresh clone.
!.gitignore
